programs.item.store.description:
A Microsoft Store app. Opens what you can do with it: repair it or reset it.
• Package · {name}
• Version · {version}

programs.repair.description:
Registers the app again from its own files, without touching its data. It fixes an app that stopped opening or lost its Start menu entry. If it still fails, try resetting it.
• Package · {name}
• Version · {version}

programs.reset.description:
Deletes the local data and settings of the app and leaves it as freshly installed, without uninstalling it. Data kept in the cloud (your account) is not touched. It asks for confirmation first. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Package · {name}
• Version · {version}

programs.uninstall.description:
Opens the program's own uninstaller, which does the work and may ask for administrator rights itself. Caduceus cannot undo it: to get the program back you must install it again. Caduceus waits until the uninstaller closes, and nothing else can be done meanwhile. Leftover files and registry entries are not touched.
• Name · {name}
• Publisher · {publisher}
• Version · {version}
• Installed · {installed}
• Uninstaller · {command}

programs.uninstall.protected.description:
Opens the program's own uninstaller. Windows or other programs depend on drivers, runtimes and redistributables, so removing one can break them. Only available with Safe mode OFF.
• Name · {name}
• Publisher · {publisher}
• Version · {version}
• Installed · {installed}
• Uninstaller · {command}

programs.uninstall.stale.description:
The uninstaller of this program and the folder it was installed in no longer exist (it was probably deleted by hand), so it cannot be uninstalled. Choosing it cleans that leftover instead: after you confirm, it removes the program's entry from the list of installed programs. No files are deleted, and a backup of the entry is saved first.
• Name · {name}
• Publisher · {publisher}
• Version · {version}
• Installed · {installed}
• Missing · {location}
• Uninstaller · {command}

